# UI test: a character that is not part of the language (SC0001).
#
# §4.2 says what Science's lexis is made of and §9 fixes only the range,
# SC0001-SC0099; the lexer allocated the first number in it for the
# catch-all. The lexer does not stop: it emits an `Unknown` token and keeps
# going, which is why all three characters below are reported.
#
# The last one is the interesting case. `!` begins no operator at all now
# that `syntax-revision-2.md` §1 has removed `!=`, and §4.3's table spells
# negation `not`. A `!` therefore lands in SC0001, but with its own message
# and an applicable fix rather than the catch-all one `$` gets.

function main():
    let priced be 100 $ 2
    let quoted be `backtick`
    let inverted be !true
